/* Your CSS for /opennms/topology.
   ./topo.sh deploys it as jetty-webapps/opennms/svg/zz-topology-styles.svg: OpenNMS puts every svg
   file of that folder into the topology page, so these rules apply there. Start a rule with "svg" to
   win over the stock stylesheet (reference/topo_default-styles.css), and a rule for a part of an icon
   with the id of its drawing (./topo.sh css <icon id> prints such rules).
   To see a change: open the page in a new tab after the first deploy of this file, then reload.
   Production gets this file only with ./topo.sh deploy prod; ./topo.sh css prod says whether it has
   your latest version and serves it. FILES.md, section 6, lists what OpenNMS draws; examples 07-09
   and 12 add rules here. The guide, steps 6.2 and 6.4, shows a label that names the version a page
   has, and ./topo.sh pagecheck says what the page loaded. */
